# Allow-list: `dof adopt` imports only these paths from ~/.claude.
#
# ~/.claude mixes configuration with machine-local state — projects/ holds full
# transcripts of every session. This list is the first gate; .dofignore is the
# second. Add a line for anything else you want synced.
#
# Matching is segment-aware (see path_matches in bin/dof):
#   settings.json   top level only    — NOT plugins/settings.json
#   *.sh            top level only    — NOT shell-snapshots/x.sh
#   commands/       that whole subtree
#
# A bare "*.sh" used to sweep in shell-snapshots/, jobs/ and plugins/ scripts,
# because shell's case-glob lets "*" cross "/". Hence the anchoring above.

# ── Instructions and settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────
CLAUDE.md
settings.json
keybindings.json

# ── Status line. If settings.json points at it, use a path starting with
#    $HOME or ~ — never a literal /home/... or /Users/..., which breaks on the
#    other platform.
statusline.sh

# ── Things you author ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
commands/
skills/
agents/
hooks/
output-styles/
scripts/
